  "findings": [
    "The complete-pipeline carrier contrast reproduces the historical feature18 versus forecast difference: about 1.406 bits of decoder cross entropy. All four circuit differences have the same sign; exact two-sided sign-flip p = 0.125. This remains exploratory and does not establish objective superiority.",
    "Native, projected and unquantized controls show that projection and readout materially affect accessibility: feature18 improves from 10/12 correct at native width to 12/12 at unquantized d8, then 11/12 at B32. Discarding coordinates can improve a fitted decoder without increasing true information.",
    "Masked native pooled carrier accuracy is 7/12 and falls to 5/12 after d8 projection; forecast native accuracy is 4/12 and falls to 2/12. Quantized rows alone cannot attribute these differences to training objectives.",
    "The forecast full-token raw readout reaches 6/12 carrier contexts, but remains 2/12 at the same d8/B32 code budget. Token width 128, the full 63 x 128 sequence, the pooled 128-vector, and the fixed 512-vector are distinct objects.",
    "The 84 low-label carrier rows are unavailable because eight labels cannot cover three classes across four training circuits. Feature18 d32 is explicitly unsupported. No dimensions or missing class results were fabricated.",
    "State, EEG and representation covariance spectra describe declared sampled populations. Finite-half mean-response cross covariance retains negative eigenvalues and is never silently projected onto a positive-semidefinite matrix."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Four evaluation circuits and 12 rhythmic contexts, all already inspected; repeated futures and optimizer repeats do not increase the independent sample size.",
    "Few-label budgets concern downstream decoder labels, not total upstream encoder supervision.",
    "The bootstrap interval is exploratory and has weak small-circuit guarantees; the exact p-value remains 0.125.",
    "Class cross entropy measures this fitted decoder, not total mutual information.",
    "CPU inference differs slightly from original CUDA float32 inference. Original pooled arrays remain unchanged; comparisons from the same recomputed tokens are saved separately.",
    "The prospective 832 episodes and full three-repeat encoder diagnostics remain unrun. Optional common-event and phase-diffusion biological runs remain unrun."
  ],
